-- title:
--   CRT reversal interface CrtNeed6 at every admissible round-six parameter record
-- statement:
--   For every round-six parameter record $P$ with $P.\mathrm{Ok}$, the interface `CrtNeed6 P` holds: for every one-entry table `tab` that provides the bit network's swap procedure (`IL.SwapNeedτ tab P.τ`) and the compact-controls row addition (`IL2.RowUCP 576 P.τ tab`), there is an extension of the IL table with entry points $e_F,e_B$ implementing the maps $\Phi$ and $\Phi^{-1}$ of the CRT step (§9.3; `KFU.PhiD`/`KFU.PhiInvD` between digits in the k-order source shape and the padded reversed box) on stack 0, with descriptor `descPhi6` on a stack $d_S\neq 0$, all other managed stacks empty and the unmanaged part preserved, for all sizes $n\ge n_1$ and valid sources (`SrcOK6`), at cost at most $C_0\,\mathrm{cU6}(P,n,A)$. The CRT axis reversal uses $3\ell$ permuted selected-bit additions with compact controls (cost row $\ell(d\ln p)^\tau$); the prefix moves and padding cost $O(Vd)$.
